1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:08,900
Hi everyone. My name is Dima, and I'm the author of the BananaShot app.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:16,900
Let me show you how to turn your match recording into a great video

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:24,900
with a scoreboard and with the time between the points cut out. For example,

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:36,900
like this video on my YouTube channel: it has a nice scoreboard, and the time between the points is gone.

5
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,900
Let's look at the app.

6
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:47,900
We start by importing our match, our video.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:55,900
Click Import new match and select the video files.

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,900
Give the project a name, so that it's clear what it is,

9
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:11,900
for example, like this. The sport is tennis. And create the project.

10
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:19,900
The app asks for the names of the players and their colors. Let me type the names

11
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:26,900
and quickly cover them here in the video. You can see that

12
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:32,900
I play in a green shirt, so I choose green for myself.

13
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:39,900
And for my opponent, I choose gray.

14
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:49,900
Here you can also change the format of the automatic scoring, or choose fully manual scoring.

15
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:56,900
What's next? Next, I need to find the moment where my

16
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:04,900
match starts. I can quickly scroll along the timeline like this. Here the previous match ends.

17
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:15,900
And here is the warm-up. And it looks like the match is about to start.

18
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:22,900
Here we find the start. Let's see.

19
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:31,900
I look for the moment when the first point starts, and I press the Point start button, or Enter on the keyboard.

20
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:39,900
The point starts. I can watch how it goes.

21
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,900
Here, you see, the first serve goes into the net.

22
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:55,900
I move the start of the point to the current moment. I just press the same button again, because I don't want to keep the first serve that went into the net.

23
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:04,900
So the point has started. Oops, I lost the point. I stop the video

24
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:13,900
and mark that Vika won this point. The scoreboard shows up right away.

25
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:19,900
And if we play the video again, you can see that after the point she has 15, and I have zero.

26
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:25,900
Let's mark one more point.

27
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:33,900
You see, I can move the video forward and back with the left and right arrow keys.

28
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:43,900
I find the moment when Vika starts to serve. I press Point start, Enter again.

29
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:51,900
And I won the point. I can click "Dima scored" or press Q. The point goes to me.

30
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:56,900
The scoreboard shows 15-15.

31
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:04,900
We can go on and mark the whole video like this. We can also choose the scoreboard style.

32
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,900
There are different scoreboard styles. For example, this one.

33
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:13,900
We can put the scoreboard in a different position. For example, on the left.

34
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:22,900
We can choose any scoreboard that we like, for example, this one, and adjust it,

35
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:29,900
for example, change the size, the transparency, the colors, or something else.

36
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:39,900
Also, if the video is a bit tilted, like here, or we don't like the colors, we can always edit it a little.

37
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:44,900
We go to the Colors & Transform tab.

38
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:56,900
Here we can change the colors, the brightness, the contrast, and make the colors less or more saturated.

39
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:05,900
We can also crop or rotate the video. For example, I want to zoom in a bit. I can do it like this.

40
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:11,900
And I can fine-tune the rotation with this slider.

41
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:19,900
I check the baseline. Yes, this looks right. Now, if we go back here, our video

42
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:30,900
already has these settings: the crop and the colors.

43
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:41,900
So we mark the whole video. And here I have a video with all the points marked. You can see that there are a lot of them.

44
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:47,900
There are 98 here. And at the end of the video, we see the final score.

45
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:57,900
When the video is ready, I can first look at the statistics of the points and the serves.

46
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:05,900
And I can choose which of them go into the final video, as a card like this.

47
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:11,900
When I'm ready, I go to the Export tab and export my videos.

48
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:18,900
Here I can choose what to export and how. For example, I can export the full video,

49
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:26,900
or only the points, or only my favorite points that I marked.

50
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:34,900
I can turn on or off the scoreboard, the comments, which you can also add to the video in

51
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:39,900
the editor, and the statistics.

52
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:48,900
Next, I choose the quality: the original quality or a lower one.

53
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:56,900
And I can fine-tune it, down to the bitrate and the encoder.

54
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:09,900
When I'm ready, I click Start export and choose the video file to export to. The app creates a new file.

55
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,900
The export starts.

56
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:20,900
And for the same project, I can choose other options. For example,

57
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:26,900
here I changed it to points. I can add it to the queue.

58
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:33,900
Then my second video starts when the first one is done. I can leave the computer on overnight, or I can

59
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:42,900
go and work on another project, and the export of this project goes on.

60
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:49,900
That's how BananaShot works. The app also has a Feedback button.

61
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:55,900
Here you can leave any ideas or questions.

62
00:07:56,000 --> 00:08:06,900
You can leave your contact for a reply if you want. I'll be very grateful for all your opinions and wishes.

63
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:11,900
See you soon. Bye, everyone!

